<!doctype html><html lang="en-CA"><head><meta charset="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width"/><title>Programs | PictureThis Production</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Fraunces:wght@400;600&family=Archivo:wght@400;600&display=swap"/><style is:global>:root{--color-ground:#FAF7F2;--color-surface:#FFFFFF;--color-elevated:#F1E8D8;--color-ink:#221A12;--color-muted:#6F6050;--color-faint:#8A7B68;--color-accent:#D98E1E;--color-accent-soft:#FDEBC8;--color-on-accent:#1C1305;--color-line:#E2D6C2;--color-civic:#203DA5;--color-civic-soft:#EEF2FC;--color-civic-ink:#14265B;--color-civic-muted:#536185;--color-civic-line:#CCD5ED;--radius-card:18px;--radius-pill:999px;--radius-ngo:4px;--spacing-page:72px;--spacing-section:88px;--spacing-block:32px;--spacing-item:24px;--spacing-tight:16px;--font-display:Fraunces, Georgia, serif;--font-body:Archivo, Helvetica, sans-serif;--font-ngo:DM Sans, sans-serif;--font-civic:Space Grotesk, sans-serif;--text-hero:64px;--text-h1:52px;--text-h2:32px;--text-h3:20px;--text-body:16px;--text-small:13px;--text-poster:88px;--text-lead:24px}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:var(--color-ground);color:var(--color-ink);font:16px/1.65 var(--font-body)}a{color:inherit}header,footer{padding:24px 5%;border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-line)}nav{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:20px;margin-top:18px}main>section,article{padding:64px 5%}h1,h2{font-family:var(--font-display);line-height:1.1}h1{font-size:clamp(38px,5vw,64px)}h2{font-size:38px}p{max-width:850px}img{max-width:100%;object-fit:cover}figure{margin:32px 0}figure img{width:100%;max-height:480px}figcaption,small{color:var(--color-muted);font-size:13px}.row{border-top:1px solid var(--color-line);padding:24px 0}input,select,textarea{display:block;width:100%;padding:14px;margin:8px 0 20px;border:1px solid var(--color-muted);font:inherit}button,.button{display:inline-block;padding:14px 24px;background:var(--color-ink);color:var(--color-ground)}:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--color-civic);outline-offset:4px}@media(max-width:760px){section{grid-template-columns:1fr!important;padding:32px 5%!important;gap:24px!important}h1{font-size:42px!important}header{display:block!important}main>div{flex-wrap:wrap;gap:16px}section>div{max-width:100%}}</style></head><body><a href="#main">Skip to content</a><header><a href="/"><b>PICTURETHIS PRODUCTION</b></a><nav><a href="//">Home</a><a href="/programs/">Programs</a><a href="/faithfire/">Faithfire</a><a href="/projects/">Projects</a><a href="/blog/">Blog</a><a href="/events/">Events</a><a href="/partners/">Partners</a><a href="/get-involved/">Get Involved</a><a href="/donate/">Donate</a></nav></header><main id="main"><section id="programs" style="padding:64px var(--spacing-page);background:var(--color-surface)"><div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:end;margin-bottom:var(--spacing-block)"><div><p style="font-size:var(--text-small);letter-spacing:.12em;color:var(--color-muted)">PROGRAMS / TRAINING · MENTORING · PATHWAYS · PRODUCTION MANAGEMENT · TECHNICAL MANAGEMENT</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:var(--text-h1);line-height:1.15;margin-top:var(--spacing-tight)">Eight weeks. Real skills.</h2></div><p style="max-width:350px;color:var(--color-muted)">Everyone starts at week 1 together.<br>Nobody is behind.</p></div><div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:56px"><div><div class="row"><small>WK 01</small><h3>Cables, connectors and signal flow</h3><p>Coil, tape and test every cable type we own. Follow a signal from microphone to speaker and find the break we hid in it.</p></div><div class="row"><small>WK 02</small><h3>Digital consoles: the Wing and X32</h3><p>Build a show file from empty: inputs, gains, EQ, routing, scenes. The two consoles most GTA rooms actually run.</p></div><div class="row"><small>WK 03</small><h3>Mixing a live band</h3><p>Soundcheck a real band at Faithfire. Vocals first, then everything else. Learn what to do when it feeds back anyway.</p></div><div class="row"><small>WK 04</small><h3>Cameras and video switching (ATEM)</h3><p>Frame, focus and follow. Then sit in the director’s chair and call a two-camera rehearsal on comms.</p></div></div><div><div class="row"><small>WK 05</small><h3>Lighting: rigging safely, running a desk</h3><p>Hang, focus and cable a rig without hurting anyone. Program cues and run a service from the lighting desk.</p></div><div class="row"><small>WK 06</small><h3>Streaming, lyrics and media</h3><p>Build a full ProPresenter service file: lyrics, scripture, sermon slides, stream output. Advance it live, on the director’s call.</p></div><div class="row"><small>WK 07</small><h3>Show calling, comms and event etiquette</h3><p>Call a show start to finish. Comms discipline, dress codes, client manners — the conduct half of the job.</p></div><div class="row"><small>WK 08</small><h3>Capstone: crew a real production</h3><p>A full event, crewed entirely by the cohort, mentors on comms only if needed. This is the reference you graduate with.</p></div></div></div><div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:56px;margin-top:var(--spacing-item);padding-top:var(--spacing-item);border-top:1px solid var(--color-line)"><p><b>Mentoring that takes care.</b> All mentors are screened with a Vulnerable Sector Check, work to a written code of conduct, and meet participants in crew spaces, never alone off-site.</p><p><b>Pathways, not promises.</b> We don’t promise jobs. We promise hours on real gear, a reference from people the industry knows, and a crew that will say your name when a call comes in.</p><p><b>Run the whole show.</b> Production Management. The other half of putting on a show: advancing the event, building the run sheet and call sheets, managing the budget, and calling the show on the day. Participants who work well on a crew learn to run the production, not just handle one role in it.</p><p><b>Lead the department.</b> Technical Management. For those who go on to lead a department: planning the rig, choosing and maintaining the gear, signing off on safety, and teaching the next cohort. It's the top of the pathway, the people who spec out the room and are accountable for it.</p></div><div style="margin-top:var(--spacing-block);padding-top:var(--spacing-item);border-top:1px solid var(--color-line)"><p style="font-size:var(--text-small);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:700;color:var(--color-muted)">Our standards</p><ul style="margin:var(--spacing-tight) 0 0;padding-left:20px;color:var(--color-muted)"><li>Every mentor passes a Vulnerable Sector Check before working with participants and follows a written code of conduct.</li><li>Mentors and participants meet in crew spaces, never alone off-site.</li><li>Participants aged 16 and 17 join with a parent or guardian's consent.</li><li>Photos and recordings of participants are used only with consent, which can be withdrawn at any time.</li><li>The program is free, and it stays free. No fees, no gear purchases, no paid upsells.</li></ul></div><figure style="margin:var(--spacing-block) 0 0"><img src="https://doop.design/photos/pexels/8412361.jpeg?h=650&w=940" alt="Two camera operators filming an indoor live event" style="width:100%;height:430px;object-fit:cover;border-radius:var(--radius-ngo)"><figcaption style="font-size:var(--text-small);color:var(--color-muted);margin-top:8px">Hands on the gear. Part of a real crew. · Illustrative photography</figcaption></figure></section><section><p>Ages 16–29 · Free — always · Saturdays 10:00 AM–2:00 PM · Next cohort: January · Bring nothing. Gear is provided.</p><p>Cohort size is twenty, and the course runs at Faithfire Production, 139 Millwick Dr, and partner venues.</p></section></main><footer><p>Training: Faithfire Production, 139 Millwick Dr, Toronto.</p><p>PictureThis Production is being set up as a nonprofit organization in Ontario.</p><p>Faithfire Production is its production arm.</p><a href="/policies/">Our standards & policies</a> · <a href={"mailto:"+contactEmail}>{contactEmail}</a> · Placeholder contact</footer></body></html>